     "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Harper%27s_Ferry_insurrection-The_U.S._Marines_storming_the_engine_house-Insurgents_firing_through_holes_in_the_doors_-_from_a_sketch_made_on_the_spot_by_our_special_artist._LCCN00652046.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Ninety Marines from the Washington barracks, under Lieutenant Israel Greene and with Army Lieutenant Colonel **Robert E. Lee** in overall command, stormed the engine house where the abolitionist John Brown had barricaded himself. Brown's raid and execution pushed the nation toward civil war.\n\n**Read more:** [John Brown's raid on Harpers Ferry — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Brown%27s_raid_on_Harpers_Ferry)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons ([file page](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Harper%27s_Ferry_insurrection-The_U.S._Marines_storming_the_engine_house-Insurgents_firing_through_holes_in_the_doors_-_from_a_sketch_made_on_the_spot_by_our_special_artist._LCCN00652046.jpg)).*"
   }
  },
  {
