    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1958_Lebanon_crisis"
    ],
    "description": "At the request of President Camille Chamoun, Marines landed at Beirut's beaches, to the surprise of sunbathers, in the first application of the Eisenhower Doctrine. Some 14,000 US troops were ashore at the peak; they left in October.\n\n**Read more:** [1958 Lebanon crisis — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1958_Lebanon_crisis)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*"
   }
  },
