    ],
    "description": "In the Battle of Ganjgal, Corporal Meyer drove into an ambush five times against orders, rescuing wounded Afghan and American troops and recovering the bodies of four fallen Americans. He was the first living Marine to receive the **Medal of Honor** since Vietnam.\n\n**Read more:** [Dakota Meyer — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakota_Meyer)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*"
