    ],
    "description": "After an executive order by President Roosevelt opened the Corps to Black Americans, about **20,000** trained at the segregated Camp Montford Point in North Carolina until 1949. In 2012 the Montford Point Marines received the **Congressional Gold Medal**.\n\n**Read more:** [Montford Point Marines — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montford_Point_Marine_Association)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons ([file page](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montford_Point_Marines_430401-M-XX999-031.jpg)).*"
