    ],
    "description": "Johnson was the first of some 300 women who enlisted in the Marine Corps Reserve in World War I, \"to free a man to fight\", working as clerks at Headquarters and elsewhere.\n\n**Read more:** [Opha May Johnson — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opha_May_Johnson)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*"
