    ],
    "description": "Lejeune approved **Operation Plan 712**, in which Major Earl \"Pete\" Ellis predicted a war with Japan and the island-by-island amphibious campaign the Marines would need to win it: a remarkably accurate forecast of the Pacific War. Ellis died in the Japanese-held Palau Islands in 1923.\n\n**Read more:** [Earl Hancock Ellis — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earl_Hancock_Ellis)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*"
