    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chosin_Reservoir"
    ],
    "description": "The Chinese blew the bridge at Funchilin Pass, below Koto-ri, the one gap no vehicle could cross. Eight Air Force C-119s parachuted in bridge sections, and engineers assembled them on **9 December**, opening the road to the sea.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Chosin Reservoir — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chosin_Reservoir)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (the treadway bridge at Funchilin Pass, 9 December 1950; U.S. Army photo).*"
