    ],
    "title": "American Revolutionary War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Revolutionary_War"
    ],
    "description": "The war for American independence, from **Lexington and Concord** to the **Treaty of Paris**.\n\nThe Continental Marines, raised in November 1775, fought aboard Continental Navy ships, landed at **New Providence (Nassau)**, and served with Washington's army at **Trenton and Princeton**. Both the Continental Navy and its Marines were disbanded after the war.\n\n**Read more:** [American Revolutionary War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Revolutionary_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Surrender_of_Lord_Cornwallis.jpg/960px-Surrender_of_Lord_Cornwallis.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "penobscot",
   "end": "-6007910400/1",
   "start": "-6009724800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "revolution",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Penobscot Expedition",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penobscot_Expedition"
    ],
    "description": "The largest American naval expedition of the Revolution, against a British post in present-day Maine.\n\nContinental and Massachusetts Marines **stormed the bluffs of Majabigwaduce** on 28 July 1779, but the expedition stalled and was destroyed when a British relief fleet arrived.\n\n**Read more:** [Penobscot Expedition — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penobscot_Expedition)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/PenobscotExpeditionBySerres.jpg/960px-PenobscotExpeditionBySerres.jpg"
   }
  },
