    "title": "Quasi-War with France",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quasi-War"
    ],
    "description": "An undeclared naval war with France over attacks on American shipping. The newly re-established Marine Corps served aboard the frigates of the young US Navy, fighting in ship-to-ship actions and boarding parties in the Caribbean.\n\n**Read more:** [Quasi-War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quasi-War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/USSConstellationVsInsurgente.jpg/960px-USSConstellationVsInsurgente.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-barbary",
   "end": "-5193072000/1",
   "start": "-5321980800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "barbary"
    ],
    "title": "First Barbary War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Barbary_War"
    ],
    "description": "Fought against Tripoli over tribute and the capture of American sailors. It gave the Marines' Hymn its line **\"to the shores of Tripoli\"** and, tradition holds, the Mameluke sword carried by Marine officers.\n\n**Read more:** [First Barbary War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Barbary_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/EnterpriseTripoli.jpg/960px-EnterpriseTripoli.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-1812",
   "end": "-4887302400/1",
   "start": "-4971456000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war"
    ],
    "title": "War of 1812",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_1812"
    ],
    "description": "War with Britain. Marines served at sea (including aboard USS *Constitution*), on the Great Lakes, at **Bladensburg** in defense of Washington, and at **New Orleans**.\n\n**Read more:** [War of 1812 — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_1812)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/War_of_1812_Montage.jpg/960px-War_of_1812_Montage.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "henderson-tenure",
   "end": "-3502396800/1",
   "start": "-4708540800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "leader",
     "commandant"
    ],
    "title": "Archibald Henderson as Commandant",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Henderson"
    ],
    "description": "The longest-serving Commandant: almost **39 years**, until his death in office. Henderson defeated a move to fold the Marines into the Army, and is remembered as the \"Grand Old Man of the Marine Corps\".\n\n**Read more:** [Archibald Henderson — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Henderson)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Archibald_Henderson.jpg/960px-Archibald_Henderson.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-seminole",
   "end": "-4019846400/1",
   "start": "-4229452800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war"
    ],
    "title": "Second Seminole War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Seminole_War"
    ],
    "description": "Henderson volunteered a Marine regiment for service in the Creek and Seminole campaigns in 1836, leading it in person in Florida and Georgia: half of the Corps' strength at the time.\n\n**Read more:** [Second Seminole War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Seminole_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/Pilaklikaha.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-mexico",
   "end": "-3847219200/1",
   "start": "-3903206400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war"
    ],
    "title": "Mexican–American War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican%E2%80%93American_War"
    ],
    "description": "Marines fought in California, along both coasts of Mexico, and with Winfield Scott's army on the march to **Mexico City**, where they took part in the storming of **Chapultepec** and stood guard at the National Palace: \"the Halls of Montezuma\".\n\n**Read more:** [Mexican–American War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican%E2%80%93American_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Nebel_Mexican_War_12_Scott_in_Mexico_City_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Nebel_Mexican_War_12_Scott_in_Mexico_City_%28cropped%29.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-civil",
   "end": "-3300912000/1",
   "start": "-3430944000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "civil war"
    ],
    "title": "American Civil War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War"
    ],
    "description": "The Union Marine Corps, never more than about 4,000 strong, served mostly at sea and in landing parties along the Confederate coast. Many officers resigned to join the small **Confederate States Marine Corps**.\n\n**Read more:** [American Civil War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Battle_of_Gettysburg%2C_by_Currier_and_Ives.png/960px-Battle_of_Gettysburg%2C_by_Currier_and_Ives.png"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-spain",
   "end": "-2252707200/1",
   "start": "-2262556800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war"
    ],
    "title": "Spanish–American War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish%E2%80%93American_War"
    ],
    "description": "A short war that made the United States a Pacific and Caribbean power. Marines seized **Guantánamo Bay** as an advanced base for the fleet: a preview of the Corps' 20th-century amphibious mission.\n\n**Read more:** [Spanish–American War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish%E2%80%93American_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Collage_infobox_for_Spanish-American_War.jpg/960px-Collage_infobox_for_Spanish-American_War.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-philippines",
   "end": "-2130019200/1",
   "start": "-2237587200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war"
    ],
    "title": "Philippine–American War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippine%E2%80%93American_War"
    ],
    "description": "Marines garrisoned bases such as Cavite and Olongapo and campaigned on Samar. Fighting continued in places long after the war was officially declared over in July 1902.\n\n**Read more:** [Philippine–American War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippine%E2%80%93American_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Manila646_1899.jpg/960px-Manila646_1899.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "boxer-legations",
   "end": "-2189548800/1",
   "start": "-2194300800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "boxer rebellion"
    ],
    "title": "Siege of the International Legations (Peking)",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_the_International_Legations"
    ],
    "description": "During the Boxer Rebellion, a small legation guard of US Marines helped hold the foreign quarter of Peking for 55 days until relief arrived.\n\nPrivate **Dan Daly** earned the first of his two Medals of Honor defending the Tartar Wall.\n\n**Read more:** [Siege of the International Legations — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_the_International_Legations)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Siege_of_Peking%2C_Boxer_Rebellion.jpg/960px-Siege_of_Peking%2C_Boxer_Rebellion.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "occupation-nicaragua",
   "end": "-1167523200/1",
   "start": "-1811721600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "banana wars",
     "occupation"
    ],
    "title": "US occupation of Nicaragua",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_occupation_of_Nicaragua"
    ],
    "description": "Part of the **Banana Wars**. Marines fought Augusto César Sandino's insurgency from 1927 and trained the Nicaraguan National Guard; future leaders such as **Chesty Puller** and **Merritt Edson** learned small-unit and air-ground tactics here.\n\n**Read more:** [United States occupation of Nicaragua — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_occupation_of_Nicaragua)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/U.S._Marines_holding_Sandino%27s_Flag_-_Nicaragua_1932.jpg/960px-U.S._Marines_holding_Sandino%27s_Flag_-_Nicaragua_1932.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "veracruz",
   "end": "-1739059200/1",
   "start": "-1757721600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "banana wars",
     "occupation"
    ],
    "title": "Occupation of Veracruz",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Veracruz_(1914)"
    ],
    "description": "Sailors and Marines landed and seized the Mexican port after the Tampico Affair. Major **Smedley Butler** received his first Medal of Honor for the fighting on 21–22 April.\n\n**Read more:** [United States occupation of Veracruz — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Veracruz_(1914))\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/LC-DIG-GGBAIN-15834_%2817523460795%29.jpg/960px-LC-DIG-GGBAIN-15834_%2817523460795%29.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "occupation-haiti",
   "end": "-1117756800/1",
   "start": "-1717718400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "banana wars",
     "occupation"
    ],
    "title": "US occupation of Haiti",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_occupation_of_Haiti"
    ],
    "description": "A 19-year occupation. Marines fought the **Caco Wars** and organized the Haitian Gendarmerie. The occupation remains controversial for its forced labor and the suppression of Haitian resistance.\n\n**Read more:** [United States occupation of Haiti — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_occupation_of_Haiti)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/American_Marines_In_1915_defending_the_entrance_gate_in_Cap-Haitian_-_34510.jpg/960px-American_Marines_In_1915_defending_the_entrance_gate_in_Cap-Haitian_-_34510.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "occupation-dominican",
   "end": "-1429142400/1",
   "start": "-1692489600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "banana wars",
     "occupation"
    ],
    "title": "US occupation of the Dominican Republic",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_Government_of_Santo_Domingo",
     "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:US_Marines_camp_in_the_Dominican_Republic.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "A US military government ran the country for eight years, with Marines fighting guerrillas in the east and building a constabulary that later became the base of Rafael Trujillo's power.\n\n**Read more:** [United States occupation of the Dominican Republic (1916–1924) — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_Government_of_Santo_Domingo)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons ([file page](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:US_Marines_camp_in_the_Dominican_Republic.jpg)).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/US_Marines_camp_in_the_Dominican_Republic.jpg/960px-US_Marines_camp_in_the_Dominican_Republic.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-ww1",
   "end": "-1613865600/1",
   "start": "-1664323200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "world war i"
    ],
    "title": "World War I (United States)",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_I",
     "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teufel_Hunden_US_Marines_recruiting_poster.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The 4th Marine Brigade fought with the Army's 2nd Division in France: **Belleau Wood**, Soissons, **Saint-Mihiel**, **Blanc Mont** and the Meuse–Argonne. The Corps grew from about 13,000 to over 70,000 Marines.\n\n**Read more:** [World War I — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_I)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons ([file page](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teufel_Hunden_US_Marines_recruiting_poster.jpg)).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/Teufel_Hunden_US_Marines_recruiting_poster.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "belleau-wood",
   "end": "-1625788800/1",
   "start": "-1627948800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war i"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Belleau Wood",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Belleau_Wood"
    ],
    "description": "Three weeks of fighting through a square mile of forest northwest of Château-Thierry, with more than 1,000 Marine casualties on **6 June** alone, then the bloodiest day in the Corps' history.\n\nThe French renamed the wood **\"Bois de la Brigade de Marine\"**. Marine legend holds the Germans called the Marines *Teufelshunde*, \"devil dogs\".\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Belleau Wood — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Belleau_Wood)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/US_Army_Infantrymen%2C_2nd_Infantry_Division%2C_Battle_of_Belleau_Wood%2C_June_1918.jpg/960px-US_Army_Infantrymen%2C_2nd_Infantry_Division%2C_Battle_of_Belleau_Wood%2C_June_1918.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "blanc-mont",
   "end": "-1615161600/1",
   "start": "-1617235200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war i"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Blanc Mont Ridge",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Blanc_Mont_Ridge"
    ],
    "description": "The 2nd Division, under Marine Major General **John A. Lejeune**, seized a ridge in Champagne that had held for years. Marshal Pétain called it the greatest single achievement of the 1918 campaign.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Blanc Mont Ridge — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Blanc_Mont_Ridge)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Battle_of_Blanc_Mont_Ridge.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-ww2",
   "end": "-767836800/1",
   "start": "-885772800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "world war ii"
    ],
    "title": "World War II (United States)",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_War"
    ],
    "description": "From Pearl Harbor to the surrender in Tokyo Bay. Six Marine divisions and five aircraft wings fought across the Central and South Pacific; the Corps peaked at about **485,000 Marines**, and nearly 87,000 were killed or wounded.\n\n**Read more:** [Pacific War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Raising_the_Flag_on_Iwo_Jima%2C_larger_-_edit1.jpg/960px-Raising_the_Flag_on_Iwo_Jima%2C_larger_-_edit1.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "wake-island",
   "end": "-884390400/1",
   "start": "-885686400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Wake Island",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wake_Island"
    ],
    "description": "The 1st Defense Battalion and VMF-211 repelled the first Japanese landing on **11 December**, sinking two destroyers: one of the few early American successes of the war. A second, larger assault took the atoll on 23 December.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Wake Island — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wake_Island)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0f/USMC-M-Wake-17.PNG"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "guadalcanal",
   "end": "-848707200/1",
   "start": "-864777600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "campaign",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Guadalcanal campaign",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guadalcanal_campaign"
    ],
    "description": "The first major Allied offensive against Japan. The **1st Marine Division** under **Alexander Vandegrift** seized the airfield, named **Henderson Field**, and held it through months of counterattacks, naval battles and disease, supported by the \"Cactus Air Force\".\n\n**Read more:** [Guadalcanal campaign — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guadalcanal_campaign)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Marines_rest_in_the_field_on_Guadalcanal.jpg/960px-Marines_rest_in_the_field_on_Guadalcanal.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "edsons-ridge",
   "end": "-861494400/1",
   "start": "-861667200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "guadalcanal"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Edson's Ridge",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Edson%27s_Ridge"
    ],
    "description": "Raiders and paratroopers under **Merritt Edson** held a low ridge south of Henderson Field against a night assault by a Japanese brigade, saving the airfield.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Edson's Ridge — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Edson%27s_Ridge)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/EdsonsRidge.jpg/960px-EdsonsRidge.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "henderson-field",
   "end": "-857865600/1",
   "start": "-858124800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "guadalcanal"
    ],
    "title": "Battle for Henderson Field",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_for_Henderson_Field",
     "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Henderson_Field_on_Guadalcanal,_in_September_1942.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The last major Japanese ground offensive on Guadalcanal. Marines under **Chesty Puller** and soldiers of the Army's 164th Infantry broke repeated night attacks; Sergeant **John Basilone** earned the Medal of Honor.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle for Henderson Field — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_for_Henderson_Field)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons ([file page](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Henderson_Field_on_Guadalcanal,_in_September_1942.jpg)).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/View_of_Henderson_Field_on_Guadalcanal%2C_in_September_1942.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "tarawa",
   "end": "-823910400/1",
   "start": "-824169600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Tarawa",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tarawa"
    ],
    "description": "The 2nd Marine Division's assault on Betio, a fortified islet of about 300 acres. Landing craft stuck on the reef, and Marines waded hundreds of yards under fire; over 1,000 were killed in 76 hours.\n\nIts lessons reshaped amphibious doctrine: more amphibian tractors, better naval gunfire and underwater demolition teams.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Tarawa — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tarawa)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Marines_Advance_on_Japanese_Pill_Boxes%2C_Tarawa%2C_November_1943_%2810962107133%29.jpg/960px-Marines_Advance_on_Japanese_Pill_Boxes%2C_Tarawa%2C_November_1943_%2810962107133%29.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "kwajalein",
   "end": "-817689600/1",
   "start": "-817948800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Kwajalein",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Kwajalein"
    ],
    "description": "The 4th Marine Division took **Roi-Namur** in the north of the atoll while the Army took Kwajalein Island: a swift success built on the lessons of Tarawa.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Kwajalein — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Kwajalein)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Men_of_the_7th_Div_HD-SN-99-02846.jpg/960px-Men_of_the_7th_Div_HD-SN-99-02846.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "saipan",
   "end": "-804124800/1",
   "start": "-806198400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Saipan",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Saipan"
    ],
    "description": "The 2nd and 4th Marine Divisions and the Army's 27th Division, under **Holland \"Howlin' Mad\" Smith**, broke Japan's inner defense line. The capture put Tokyo within range of B-29 bombers, and its fall brought down Prime Minister Tojo's government.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Saipan — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Saipan)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Marines_and_King_Kong_on_Saipan.jpg/960px-Marines_and_King_Kong_on_Saipan.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "guam",
   "end": "-801360000/1",
   "start": "-803088000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Guam",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Guam_(1944)"
    ],
    "description": "The recapture of the first American territory taken by Japan, by the 3rd Marine Division, the 1st Provisional Marine Brigade and the Army's 77th Division.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Guam (1944) — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Guam_(1944))\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/First_flag_on_Guam_-_1944.jpg/960px-First_flag_on_Guam_-_1944.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "tinian",
   "end": "-802137600/1",
   "start": "-802828800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Tinian",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tinian"
    ],
    "description": "Often called the most nearly perfect amphibious operation of the war. Tinian's airfields later launched the atomic bombing missions against Hiroshima and Nagasaki.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Tinian — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tinian)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/A_Water_Buffalo%2C_loaded_with_Marines%2C_churns_through_the_sea_bound_for_beaches_of_Tinian_Island_near_Guam._-_NARA_-_513181.tif/lossy-page1-960px-A_Water_Buffalo%2C_loaded_with_Marines%2C_churns_through_the_sea_bound_for_beaches_of_Tinian_Island_near_Guam._-_NARA_-_513181.tif.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "peleliu",
   "end": "-791942400/1",
   "start": "-798249600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Peleliu",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Peleliu"
    ],
    "description": "Expected to last days, the battle lasted ten weeks. Japanese defenders fought from caves in the coral ridges of the Umurbrogol, and the 1st Marine Division suffered over 6,500 casualties.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Peleliu — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Peleliu)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e9/First_wave_of_LVTs_moves_toward_the_invasion_beaches_-_Peleliu.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "iwo-jima",
   "end": "-781660800/1",
   "start": "-784684800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Iwo Jima",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Iwo_Jima"
    ],
    "description": "Three Marine divisions against 21,000 defenders dug into tunnels across eight square miles of volcanic ash. Over 6,800 Americans and nearly all the Japanese garrison died.\n\n> \"Among the Americans who served on Iwo Island, uncommon valor was a common virtue.\" — Admiral Chester Nimitz\n\n27 Medals of Honor were awarded for Iwo Jima, more than for any other single battle.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Iwo Jima — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Iwo_Jima)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Raising_the_Flag_on_Iwo_Jima%2C_larger_-_edit1.jpg/960px-Raising_the_Flag_on_Iwo_Jima%2C_larger_-_edit1.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "okinawa",
   "end": "-774057600/1",
   "start": "-781142400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "world war ii",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Okinawa",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Okinawa"
    ],
    "description": "The largest amphibious assault of the Pacific War. The 1st and 6th Marine Divisions fought alongside the Army's Tenth Army through Shuri Castle and the island's south, while kamikazes struck the fleet offshore. More than 100,000 Okinawan civilians died.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Okinawa — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Okinawa)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Ww2_158.jpg/960px-Ww2_158.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-korea",
   "end": "-518572800/1",
   "start": "-616032000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "korean war"
    ],
    "title": "Korean War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_War"
    ],
    "description": "Called up at short notice after cuts that had nearly reduced it to a ceremonial force, the Corps sent the 1st Provisional Marine Brigade to the **Pusan Perimeter**, landed at **Inchon**, and fought its way out of the **Chosin Reservoir**. Marine helicopters flew the first combat medical evacuations and troop lifts.\n\n**Read more:** [Korean War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Chosin.jpg/960px-Chosin.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "pusan",
   "end": "-608688000/1",
   "start": "-612576000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "korean war"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of the Pusan Perimeter",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Pusan_Perimeter"
    ],
    "description": "The 1st Provisional Marine Brigade, a \"fire brigade\" moved wherever the line was threatened, helped hold the last United Nations foothold in Korea, notably in the battles of the Naktong Bulge.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Pusan Perimeter — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Pusan_Perimeter)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fb/27th_Infantry_Regiment_soldiers_at_the_Pusan_Perimeter%2C_September_4%2C_1950.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "inchon",
   "end": "-608601600/1",
   "start": "-608947200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "korean war",
     "amphibious"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Inchon",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Inchon"
    ],
    "description": "Douglas MacArthur's amphibious gamble far behind North Korean lines, against extreme tides and seawalls. The 1st Marine Division landed and drove on to recapture **Seoul**, cutting the North Korean army's supply lines.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Inchon — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Inchon)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Battle_of_Inchon.png/960px-Battle_of_Inchon.png"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "chosin",
   "end": "-601257600/1",
   "start": "-602640000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "korean war"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Chosin Reservoir",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chosin_Reservoir"
    ],
    "description": "Surrounded by Chinese armies in temperatures down to −35 °F, the 1st Marine Division under **Oliver P. Smith** fought 78 miles south to the port of Hungnam, bringing out its wounded, its dead and its equipment.\n\nSurvivors are known as the **\"Chosin Few\"**.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Chosin Reservoir — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chosin_Reservoir)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Chosin.jpg/960px-Chosin.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-vietnam",
   "end": "102211200/1",
   "start": "-152064000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "vietnam war"
    ],
    "title": "Marines in the Vietnam War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War"
    ],
    "description": "From the landing at Da Nang to the last American troops leaving South Vietnam. Marines held the northern provinces of I Corps, from the DMZ to Da Nang, combining large battles with the **Combined Action Program** of rifle squads living in villages. About **13,000 Marines** died in Vietnam.\n\n**Read more:** [Vietnam War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/U.S._Army_UH-1H_Hueys_insert_ARVN_troops_at_Kh%C3%A2m_%C4%90%E1%BB%A9c%2C_Vietnam%2C_12_July_1970_%2879431435%29.jpg/960px-U.S._Army_UH-1H_Hueys_insert_ARVN_troops_at_Kh%C3%A2m_%C4%90%E1%BB%A9c%2C_Vietnam%2C_12_July_1970_%2879431435%29.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "khe-sanh",
   "end": "-46742400/1",
   "start": "-61430400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "vietnam war"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Khe Sanh",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Khe_Sanh"
    ],
    "description": "A 77-day siege of the Marine combat base near the Laotian border by two North Vietnamese divisions, broken by massive air support (Operation Niagara) and Operation Pegasus. The base was abandoned that July.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Khe Sanh — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Khe_Sanh)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3c/Khe_Sanh_Bunkers_and_burning_Fuel_Dump.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "hue",
   "end": "-57888000/1",
   "start": "-60566400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "vietnam war",
     "tet offensive"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Huế",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Hu%E1%BA%BF"
    ],
    "description": "During the Tet Offensive, Marines and South Vietnamese troops retook the ancient imperial capital house by house: the Corps' first major urban battle since Seoul in 1950. Thousands of civilians were killed, many in massacres by occupying forces.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Huế — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Hu%E1%BA%BF)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Marines_Fire_From_a_House_Window%2C_February_1968_%2816242259837%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Marines_Fire_From_a_House_Window%2C_February_1968_%2816242259837%29_%28cropped%29.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "lebanon-mnf",
   "end": "446601600/1",
   "start": "399081600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "peacekeeping",
     "lebanon"
    ],
    "title": "Multinational Force in Lebanon",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multinational_Force_in_Lebanon"
    ],
    "description": "Marines deployed to Beirut as peacekeepers with French, Italian and British contingents during the Lebanese Civil War. The mission ended months after the 1983 barracks bombing.\n\n**Read more:** [Multinational Force in Lebanon — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multinational_Force_in_Lebanon)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/AH-1T_SeaCobra_in_the_outskirts_of_Beirut_1983.JPEG/960px-AH-1T_SeaCobra_in_the_outskirts_of_Beirut_1983.JPEG"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-gulf",
   "end": "667699200/1",
   "start": "649555200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "gulf war"
    ],
    "title": "Gulf War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_War"
    ],
    "description": "After Iraq invaded Kuwait, more than **90,000 Marines** deployed for Operations Desert Shield and Desert Storm, the largest Marine operation since World War II. An amphibious force afloat held Iraqi divisions on the coast while the 1st and 2nd Marine Divisions breached the defenses into Kuwait.\n\n**Read more:** [Gulf War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/USAF_F-16A_F-15C_F-15E_Desert_Storm_edit2.jpg/960px-USAF_F-16A_F-15C_F-15E_Desert_Storm_edit2.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "desert-storm-ground",
   "end": "667699200/1",
   "start": "667353600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "campaign",
     "gulf war"
    ],
    "title": "Desert Storm ground offensive",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberation_of_Kuwait_campaign"
    ],
    "description": "The \"100-hour\" ground war. Marine divisions breached two belts of minefields and obstacles and reached Kuwait City's outskirts and Kuwait International Airport.\n\n**Read more:** [Liberation of Kuwait campaign — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberation_of_Kuwait_campaign)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/An_Iraqi_T-54%2C_T-55_or_Type_59_and_T-55A_on_Basra-Kuwait_Highway_near_Kuwait.JPEG/960px-An_Iraqi_T-54%2C_T-55_or_Type_59_and_T-55A_on_Basra-Kuwait_Highway_near_Kuwait.JPEG"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-afghanistan",
   "end": "1630281600/1",
   "start": "1002412800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "afghanistan"
    ],
    "title": "War in Afghanistan",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_in_Afghanistan_(2001%E2%80%932021)"
    ],
    "description": "America's longest war. Marines seized **Camp Rhino** in 2001 and, from 2008, fought for years in **Helmand Province**, including Marjah and Sangin, before handing over to Afghan forces in 2014. They returned to secure Kabul airport for the final evacuation in 2021.\n\n**Read more:** [War in Afghanistan (2001–2021) — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_in_Afghanistan_(2001%E2%80%932021))\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/U.S._Army_firefight_in_Kunar.jpg/960px-U.S._Army_firefight_in_Kunar.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "war-iraq",
   "end": "1324166400/1",
   "start": "1048118400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "war",
     "iraq"
    ],
    "title": "Iraq War",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq_War"
    ],
    "description": "The I Marine Expeditionary Force drove from Kuwait to Baghdad and Tikrit in 2003. Marines then spent years in **Al Anbar Province**, where the Sunni tribes' **Anbar Awakening** of 2006–2007 turned against al-Qaeda in Iraq.\n\n**Read more:** [Iraq War — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq_War)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/UStanks_baghdad_2003.JPEG/960px-UStanks_baghdad_2003.JPEG"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "fallujah-1",
   "end": "1083369600/1",
   "start": "1081036800/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "iraq"
    ],
    "title": "First Battle of Fallujah",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Battle_of_Fallujah"
    ],
    "description": "Operation Vigilant Resolve, launched after the killing of four contractors in the city. Marines were ordered to halt before taking the city, which was handed to a short-lived local \"Fallujah Brigade\".\n\n**Read more:** [First Battle of Fallujah — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Battle_of_Fallujah)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/42/Npi040604a4b.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "fallujah-2",
   "end": "1103760000/1",
   "start": "1099785600/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "iraq"
    ],
    "title": "Second Battle of Fallujah",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Battle_of_Fallujah"
    ],
    "description": "Operation Phantom Fury: Marine and Army units cleared the insurgent stronghold block by block, the heaviest urban combat for US forces since **Huế** in 1968.\n\n**Read more:** [Second Battle of Fallujah — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Battle_of_Fallujah)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/4-14_Marines_in_Fallujah.jpg/960px-4-14_Marines_in_Fallujah.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "marjah",
   "end": "1291680000/1",
   "start": "1266019200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "afghanistan"
    ],
    "title": "Battle of Marjah",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Moshtarak",
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjah"
    ],
    "description": "Operation Moshtarak, the largest offensive of the Afghan war at the time: Marines and Afghan troops took a Taliban stronghold in central Helmand, then fought months of insurgency in its farmland.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Marjah — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Moshtarak)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons ([file page](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjah)).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Marines_in_poppy_fields.jpg/960px-Marines_in_poppy_fields.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "kabul-airlift",
   "end": "1630281600/1",
   "start": "1628899200/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "evacuation",
     "afghanistan"
    ],
    "title": "Kabul airlift",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Kabul_airlift"
    ],
    "description": "Marines, soldiers and allied troops held Hamid Karzai International Airport as more than **120,000 people** were evacuated after the fall of Kabul to the Taliban.\n\n**Read more:** [2021 evacuation from Afghanistan — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Kabul_airlift)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (from the article above).*",
    "backgroundUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Afghanistan_Evacuation_210821-M-GQ845-1035.jpg/960px-Afghanistan_Evacuation_210821-M-GQ845-1035.jpg"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "task-force-faith",
   "start": "-602640000/1",
   "end": "-602294400/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "korean war",
     "chosin",
     "army"
    ],
    "title": "Task Force Faith east of the reservoir",
    "iconUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Lt._Col._Don_C._Faith%2C_Jr.%2C_150226-O-ZZ999-021.jpg/960px-Lt._Col._Don_C._Faith%2C_Jr.%2C_150226-O-ZZ999-021.jpg",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chosin_Reservoir"
    ],
    "description": "East of the reservoir, the Army's **Regimental Combat Team 31** of the 7th Infantry Division, later called Task Force Faith after Lt. Col. Don C. Faith Jr., was cut off on 27 November and overrun in its attempt to break out to Hagaru-ri on 1 December. It lost more than a thousand men; survivors crossed the frozen reservoir to the Marine lines. Faith was killed and received the Medal of Honor. Chosin was not the Marines' fight alone.\n\n**Read more:** [Battle of Chosin Reservoir — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chosin_Reservoir)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (Lt. Col. Don C. Faith Jr.; U.S. Army photo).*"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "fox-company-toktong",
   "start": "-602553600/1",
   "end": "-602208000/1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "battle",
     "korean war",
     "chosin"
    ],
    "title": "Fox Company holds Toktong Pass",
    "iconUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/WilliamBarberUSMC.jpg/960px-WilliamBarberUSMC.jpg",
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_E._Barber",
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chosin_Reservoir"
    ],
    "description": "**Fox Company, 2nd Battalion, 7th Marines**, under Capt. **William E. Barber**, held the hill over Toktong Pass, the only road between Yudam-ni and Hagaru-ri, for five nights against repeated attacks. Barber, wounded, led from a stretcher and refused to withdraw. Of his 220 men, only 82 were able to walk away. He received the Medal of Honor.\n\n**Read more:** [William E. Barber — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_E._Barber)\n\n*Image: Wikimedia Commons (Capt. William E. Barber; U.S. Marine Corps photo).*"
   }
  }
 ],
